{
  "_README": "Files vendored byte-identical from the abulxt repo (same path in both trees). scripts/vendor-sync.mjs --check fails when a copy differs; --pull refreshes them from ABULXT_DIR (default ../abulxt). Change the abulxt copy first, then pull. Two groups: `files` is the client-protection pipeline; `botShared` is the server code the Discord bot shares with abulxt's app server (database, events, config, chat permissions, the AI engine /ai uses), plus the data it reads at runtime (personas, schema.sql). abulxt owns botShared until phase 1 moves the chat API; the chat API (discord-bridge-api.ts, discord-onboarding-api.ts and its helpers: discord-unfurl, discord-author-style, discord-cdn-refresh, discord-embed-suppress, discord-guild-tag, discord-mention-limits; holt-owned since 2026-10-24, deleted from abulxt) and the bot-only files (discord-service.ts, discord-bridge-bot.ts, discord-commands/, ...) are holt's and are NOT listed. chatAssets are the public files the chatbox references (fonts, Discord icons). chatClient is the chatbox UI (pages/chat and the abulxt client modules it imports, including lib/config.ts and the theme); abulxt owns it until its own copy of the chatbox is deleted. holt-owned stand-ins replace the modules that tie the chatbox to abulxt's page: lib/navigate.ts, components/AuthGate.tsx, lib/ads.ts, lib/api-base.ts (the chatbox's API is the page's own origin, or ./_holt/ for a platform with its own accounts; no backend failover). Holt-owned files that only borrow abulxt's shape (canary-list.json, obfuscation-strings.ts, lib/config.ts, holt-config.ts) are not listed either. scripts/obfuscate-build.test.mjs is deliberately NOT vendored: its fixtures are abulxt canaries and only hold against abulxt's own canary-list.json.",
